{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789959498,"nonce":"kAirx6AFm9acSaGWZyrnshEdu3A=","title":"LLVM backend seeds every instruction value with zero, so a forward reference reads 0 instead of failing","message":"compile_function and compile_osr_helper (crates/compiler/src/llvm_backend.rs) pre-seed the value map with const_zero for every HirValueKind::Instruction. A block compiled before the block defining a value it reads therefore gets 0 and keeps going; that is how 162c831 stayed invisible until a benchmark's answer changed. Seed Undef (or nothing) and make get_value fail with the HirId when an instruction value is read before its block was compiled, or gate an assertion behind ZYNTAX_CHECK_HIR_USES so an ordering regression fails loud in tests.","files":null}]}